re:node1:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity\"]}],\"confidence\":0.95,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.9,\"summary\":\"All state-changing commands map clearly to task prerequisites (installing lvm2), core deliverables (loop-backed PV/VG/LV creation, mount, grow), or persistence/restart-evidence needs (systemd unit + fstab entry to survive reboot, which was necessary since the volume depends on loop devices that must be reattached at boot). No abandoned experiments, failed services, or security-control weakening were found; failed-services and package-health observations are empty/clean in both before_prepare and after_executor snapshots. Minor residue: /tmp/dnf-lvm2.log and /tmp/reboot.log were left in /tmp (visible in the after_executor temporary-files diff) but are low-risk, bounded log artifacts from legitimate install/reboot actions, not evidence of unnecessary or destructive mutation.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node1:package-health\",\"global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files\",\"cmd-9f13cef81b3e4dc2\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"The executor satisfied all material outcomes: an LVM logical volume was created and mounted at /srv/data (<2GB initially), then grown live to ~2.34GB while remaining mounted, with data integrity verified via checksums both immediately after growth and after a full node restart. The independent node-restart evidence protocol was also completed cleanly for node1, with directly observed pre-restart baseline, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and full post-restart recovery of the LVM stack, mount, and data. The use of loop-backed devices was a reasonable adaptation given the disk had no free space for a native PV, and hygiene is clean apart from two minor log files left in /tmp.\",\"limitations\":[\"No independent verification tool was available beyond the captured evidence; all conclusions rely on the executor's own command outputs, though they are consistent with the fixed lifecycle snapshots.\",\"The volume backing store is two sparse loop-device-backed files rather than a native block device, since the disk was fully partitioned with no free space; this is a reasonable engineering workaround given the constraint but differs from a typical dedicated-disk LVM setup.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"initial-lv-mounted","requirement":"Provide a logical volume mounted at /srv/data on node1","status":"satisfied","summary":"Executor created PV/VG(datavg)/LV(datalv) on a loop-backed device (no native free space existed on the single fully-partitioned disk), formatted xfs, and mounted it at /srv/data at ~1.2GB, then wrote test data with recorded sha256 checksums.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d9768189e4984b13"]},{"id":"grow-to-2gb-while-mounted","requirement":"Grow the volume to at least 2GB while it stays mounted","status":"satisfied","summary":"A second loop-backed PV was added via vgextend, the LV was extended to <2.34GiB, and xfs_growfs was run online against the still-mounted /srv/data (mount confirmed active immediately before growfs). Post-growth lsblk shows exact size 2,508,193,792 bytes (~2.34GB), confirmed again in the pre-restart and post-restart checks.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9331c353aef84b05","cmd-58663e6f19804b70","cmd-183594b7baeb4a15"]},{"id":"contents-intact","requirement":"Contents stay intact through the resize","status":"satisfied","summary":"sha256sum -c against the pre-growth checksum manifest reported both testfile.bin and marker.txt OK immediately after the grow operation, and again after the subsequent node restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9331c353aef84b05","cmd-183594b7baeb4a15"]},{"id":"node-restart-evidence-protocol","requirement":"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol on every managed node (node1) after task completion","status":"satisfied","summary":"Pre-restart baseline captured healthy state (boot_id 1b0321bf..., vgs/lvs/pvs active, mount present, checksums 